{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\ne=d['experiment']\ne['previous_id']='cdee42fcadd7460991a44622a9725658-experiment'\ne['revision_reason']=\\\"The executed run reproduced every observation but both comparisons were scored unknown because the identity field I declared (x_index) was absent from the result events and the prerequisite event could therefore not be correlated to them. The harness now emits x_index in old_side_elected and after_heal, so the admission on silent_change (committed, entry_type_at_x=LogConfiguration) correlates with both result events; predictions, scope and prefix are unchanged, and the corrected harness was re-verified in an isolated copy of the captured tree.\\\"\ne['comparisons']=[\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_truncation\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"committed_entry_truncated\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry committed under the configuration recorded in the logs must not be replaced after the partition heals.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"old_side_elected\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"x_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_dual_leaders\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_still_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"At most one leader may exist for a given log: the old-configuration side must not elect a leader while the new-configuration side still leads.\\\"}\n]\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['executions']={'430d7ba602ed4666bdfe63a96c71e2fc':[1],'d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740':[1,3],'edfd3c204c654542a8bdb4263f290d4d':[1],'4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a':[1],'7afe8c0403874dbeb0a917a3ee9ed837':[1],'79d93a5aaad448888cc04214be8f2ad8':[2,3,4]}\ni['joint_history']=(\\\"All receipts belong to this question and were executed from the same snapshot. 430d7ba6 (empty configuration), d2d1cb09 (stale configuration and the silently dropped voter), edfd3c20 (isolated control, holds), 4f4a771f (all voters restart, cluster-wide progress loss), 7afe8c04 (live quorum cannot elect) and 79d93a5a (silent two-server change, concurrent leaders, truncation of the committed entry) form one chain: each was built from the previous receipt's outcome, and each uses the same bootstrap/commit/snapshot/restart operations rather than fabricated state.\\\")\ni['rationale']=i['rationale']+(\\\" (6) 79d93a5aaad448888cc04214be8f2ad8: with A's configuration coming from a snapshot ({A,B}) while its log holds the newer {A,B,C} entry, AddVoter E returned no error and the silently created two-server change committed at index 11 with A's commit index at 11 and E holding the same LogConfiguration entry (parsed index 2), while B stayed at log index 10 with the old membership; the old majority {B,C} then elected B in term 4 while A was still leader in term 3 (parsed index 3, a_still_leader=true), and after the partition healed A's entry 11 was a LogNoop of term 4 rather than the committed configuration entry (parsed index 4, committed_entry_truncated=true).\\\")\ni['answers']['1ed9540f22fe4fa9bef3b3bda88e22e8-gap-2']={\n \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Resolved by retained receipt 79d93a5aaad448888cc04214be8f2ad8: the silent two-server change {A,B,C} -> {A,B,E} committed on A plus the promoted caught-up nonvoter E (parsed index 2: change_err nil, x_index 11, committed=true, entry type LogConfiguration on A and on E, A commit index 11, B still at log index 10); the old majority {B,C} elected B in term 4 while A was still leader in term 3 (parsed index 3), i.e. two concurrent leaders with disjoint support over the same log; and after healing, A's entry at index 11 became a LogNoop of term 4 (parsed index 4), so the entry committed under the configuration recorded in the logs was truncated on the node that had committed it. The receipt's own comparison scoring failed because of my identity wiring (x_index was not emitted in the result events), which the successor experiment in this update corrects.\\\",\n \\\"resolved\\\":True}\ni['limitations']=[l for l in i['limitations'] if 'retained receipt is requested' not in l and 'No control variant' not in l]\ni['limitations'] += [\n \\\"Receipt 79d93a5aaad448888cc04214be8f2ad8 reproduced all dual-majority observations but scored both comparisons unknown because the declared identity field was missing from the result events; those observations are cited as parsed indices rather than as scored comparisons, and the corrected successor experiment is requested in this update.\\\",\n \\\"The dual-majority probe has no control variant: with the flag disabled the leader's configuration is current, so the same AddVoter is a single-server change and cannot create disjoint majorities (nextConfiguration over the current configuration, configuration.go 224-302).\\\"]\ni['counterevidence']=i['counterevidence']+[\n \\\"The dual-majority path needs a caught-up nonvoter E so the silent change can commit without the partitioned voter B; without such a node the change would need B's acknowledgement and B would then hold the new membership.\\\"]\nd['knowledge']=[{\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"NewRaft does not restore a configuration entry that lies inside the replayed committed log prefix: with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled the configuration comes only from the newest snapshot plus configuration entries above max(lastSnapshot, persistedCommitIndex), so a node restarted from a log whose newest configuration entry is at or below the persisted commit index adopts the snapshot configuration (empty when there is no snapshot) instead of the replicated one.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"RestoreCommittedLogs=true; LogStore implements CommitTrackingLogStore; node started on stores whose persisted commit index is at or above the newest configuration entry index; no snapshot whose ConfigurationIndex covers that entry.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"process_config_entry\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"430d7ba602ed4666bdfe63a96c71e2fc\\\":[1],\\\"d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740\\\":[1]}}]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
